The first implementation is running its full gate suite now. It uses only standard-library exact graph checks, keeps the answer at eight vertex IDs, and grows only the graph size across the main ladder. The expensive parts of this run are deliberate: 200,000 structure-aware guesses, five construction-aware attacks over eight seeds, exact branch-and-bound measurements, and 60 relabelling-invariance checks.
