/tmp/paper_2004_10596/templateArxiv.tex:278:\par Grover’s algorithm works with a unitary operator $O$ called the oracle function, which is defined by $\ket {x} \ket{q} \implies \ket{x} \ket {q \oplus f(x)}$. where $\ket{x}$ is the $n$ qubit index register and $\ket{q}$ is an additional qubit, called the oracle qubit. The functional view of Grover's Search Algorithm is presented here. 
