The complete flow of proposed design for mapping clique problem from a graph to quantum computer is shown in Figure \ref{generalflow}. The proposed algorithm \textbf{Oracle\_clique\_problem} takes adjacency matrix as input and gives an QASM gate list as output. After realizing the logical gates into quantum computer supported 1-qubit and 2-qubit gates and through qubit mapping algorithm based on qubit topology, this QASM gate list can be further used as an input to a quantum computer to get the implementation result of clique problem. These MCT realization \cite{Acasiete_2020} and qubit mapping algorithm \cite{zul8342181, li2019tackling, tan2020optimal} are well-defined in the literature. We have just adopted them as a support in our framework.


