 This is not evidence for average-case planted-clique hardness. It is a Track B benchmark whose exact branch solver is fast with tools. The 0/200,000 guess result estimates only the declared prior—uniform increasing `k`-subsets after the obvious degree filter—and is an upper-resolution observation, not proof that the valid-answer density is zero. The demo has two answers, and the verifier intentionally accepts either.
 
