 Rows 10 and 17 repeat, so their neighborhood is `{2,6,11,13}`. XORing rows 2, 6, 11, and 13 gives bits `{8,9,15,16}`. Thus `<answer>[8,9,15,16]</answer>` verifies as `(True, "ok")`. Dropping 16 gives `(False, "expected exactly 4 vertices")`. A person can solve this demo on paper with four five-digit hexadecimal XORs; exhaustive enumeration finds two valid 4-cliques.
