codex
The paper confirms the native task and exposes the crucial easy route: Section 4.2 explicitly enumerates all \(\binom{n}{k}\) vertex sets, Section 5 charges \(O(k\binom{n}{k}+k)\) oracle-synthesis gates, and Section 7 gives Grover’s \(O(\sqrt{\binom{n}{k}/m})\) iterations. It gives no average-case theorem for planted graphs, so Track A would be false; Track B is the only defensible route.

I also found one issue in the provisional implementation: its “40 operations” counts a 64-bit XOR as one mental operation. I’m measuring the compact route at the rendered hexadecimal-digit level and will adjust the shipping regime or accounting so G9 is honest.
